profession_prompt:
Marisol is a bilingual (English and Spanish) Tier 1 customer care representative. Her day is phone calls, plus
scheduled "digital blocks" for email and chat tickets, plus internal chat with her team and the other support
groups. Customers call or write about bills, payments, service problems, moves, plan changes and cancellations.

Good help in this job means:
- the right answer for this customer, from their account and the current policies, not a guess;
- identity verified before anything about an account is shared;
- offers, credits and promises that stay within what a Tier 1 rep may approve, and clean hand-offs to the team
  that owns the rest (with the details that team needs);
- complete case notes for every contact, and follow-ups that do not slip;
- a calm, clear, courteous tone, short enough to say on a call or read on a phone.
Policies and procedures are in the knowledge base; customer accounts are in the billing console records.

